+    /// cfg), so its Pippenger runs on one thread. When rayon has more than one
+    /// thread, split the input into one chunk per thread, run the unchanged
+    /// serial MSM on each chunk and add the partial results: an MSM is a sum,
+    /// so the group element is the same. Small or uneven inputs keep the
+    /// original path.
